WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.270
ROGER MARTINEZ: It is week five
of "Google Cloud Next OnAir,"

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.300
and this week, we're
focusing on data analytics.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.180
I'm Roger Martinez, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud,"

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.630
where we're taking a sneak
peek at this week's content.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.850
Week five is all
about data analytics,

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.100
meaning we want to help you
make the most of your data

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.432
by helping you efficiently
store and get insights from it.

00:00:20.432 --> 00:00:22.890
We've got sessions on everything
from storing and streaming

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.150
your data to empowering it
with real time AI, BigQuery

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.320
ML, and more.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.630
It's always exciting to hear
real world examples of how

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.670
people build on Google Cloud.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.700
Don't Sweat The Big Stuff
is a perfect example.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.640
Geotab talks about how
they use BigQuery and lots

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.460
of other tools to enable their
data science scene to analyze

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.510
petabytes of data.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.290
The key here is to let them
focus on the data and models

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.910
while letting Google's
infrastructure

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.252
handle all the heavy lifting.

00:00:50.252 --> 00:00:51.960
Now, I love to stay
on top of new updates

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.610
that make Google Cloud
tools easier to use.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.970
So my pick for the week
is awesome new features

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.125
to help you manage BigQuery.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.750
There's lots of great
ways in the Cloud

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.550
to help you wrangle your
data, but BigQuery really

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:05.830
shines this week.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.990
This talk is perfect for
newcomers and power users

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.900
alike with practical ways to
get your head around pricing,

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.735
administration, and monitoring.

00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:15.610
To round out the week,
make sure to check out

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.030
the cool demos that show what
data analytics can help you do.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:20.640
This week features
some great videos

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.530
and a cool interactive demo
that visualizes MLB pitcher

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.880
data in a 3D environment.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.660
Whether you're a sports fan,
a statistics expert, or just

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.610
like playing around
with interactive demos,

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.470
be sure to take a look.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.750
To add these sessions to
your digital playlist,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.110
check out the link.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.550
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.767
Leave us a comment or
tweet us using the hashtag

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.860
#GoogleCloudNext.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:44.550
We'll see you in the Cloud.

